<title>BRAZIL: Sao Paulo private-sector lay-offs increase in Aug.</title>
<headline>Sao Paulo private-sector lay-offs increase in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private companies in Brazil's Sao Paulo state laid off 29,331 employees in August, compared with 14,399 the previous month, the Sao Paulo State Industries Federation (Fiesp) said Monday.</p>
<p>It was the most lay-offs recorded in any month since September 1995.</p>
<p>So far this year, Sao Paulo industries have laid off 145,217 workers, or 6.79 percent of the state's industrial workforce, Fiesp said. In the past 12 months, Sao Paulo companies have laid off 252,697 workers, or 11.16 percent of the workforce.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
